WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.460
Good to have you on Planetarian Daily, episode 112.

00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:06.660
Today is July 6th, 2026.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.340
Some interesting findings to cover today.

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:12.040
A blood test measuring Apple B particles

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:13.920
may prevent more heart attacks

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:16.400
than standard LDL cholesterol screening

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.380
while staying cost effective.

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:21.580
Researchers compared Apple B particle counts

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:23.320
with standard LDL measurements

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:25.360
in large population data sets.

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:29.420
Apple B directly quantifies the atherogenic particles

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:30.900
that enter artery walls.

00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:33.400
The test remained cost effective

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:35.960
within US healthcare spending thresholds

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:38.520
while projecting fewer heart attacks and strokes.

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:41.740
Current guidelines still rely primarily

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:43.900
on LDL cholesterol values.

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:47.580
Wider adoption would require updated laboratory reference

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.500
ranges and clinician education.

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:53.700
CSIRO researchers developed Flockmate,

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:55.980
a two-year project that uses sensors

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:58.400
to capture live weight and fleece weight

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:00.860
as sheep move freely through their environment.

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:04.540
The system avoids labor-intensive manual measurements

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:07.300
that stress animals and disrupt farm routines.

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:10.640
It records data continuously rather than

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:12.360
at discrete handling events.

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:14.940
Farmers can track flock changes

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:17.000
without repeated physical interventions.

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:19.940
Next steps include field validation

00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:22.860
across different sheep breeds and pasture conditions.

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:26.360
A new systematic scheme uses machine learning

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:28.800
to classify structural changes in water

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:30.960
across temperature and pressure ranges.

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:34.940
Water expands on freezing and shows other anomalies

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:37.460
tied to shifts in its hydrogen bond network.

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:39.860
The model distinguishes ordered

00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:42.020
and disordered molecular arrangements

00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:45.120
without relying on predefined geometric templates.

00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:48.840
Validation against experimental scattering data

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:50.460
confirmed the classifications.

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:52.860
The framework can now be applied

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:54.520
to other anomalous liquids.

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:59.860
Zoologists analyzed attacks that occurred between 2020 and 2021

00:02:00.460 --> 00:02:02.960
to identify conditions that increase conflict

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:05.040
between people and urban coyotes.

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:07.400
The study documented changes

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:09.980
in coyote behavior linked to food availability

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:11.820
and human activity patterns.

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:14.980
Recommendations focus on securing garbage,

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:16.360
supervising pets,

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:19.680
and maintaining distance during known dening periods.

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:22.240
The findings apply to other cities

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:24.900
experiencing similar wildlife adaptation.

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:27.580
Ongoing monitoring will track whether

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:29.200
the measures reduce encounters.

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:33.140
Lipid droplets rich in triacylglycerols

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:34.580
and cholesterol esters

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:36.760
were shown to support precise formation

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:39.720
of super molecular polymers inside living cells.

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:42.680
The neutral lipid environment modulates

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:45.380
polymerization kinetics and polymer length.

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:48.080
Researchers varied lipid composition

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:51.020
to achieve on-demand control over assembly.

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:53.500
This mechanism offers a route

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:55.180
to regulate cellular functions

00:02:55.180 --> 00:02:56.760
through engineered polymers.

00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:59.840
Future experiments will test whether the approach

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:02.620
can deliver therapeutic cargoes within droplets.

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:06.460
Now, shifting to a very different area of research.

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:09.800
Artificial lighting at night traps woodlice

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:11.560
in continuous looping paths

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:14.440
never previously recorded in natural settings.

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:17.540
The behavior occurs when light disrupts

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:19.920
the animal's orientation cues on the ground.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:22.980
Thousands of individuals can become caught

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:24.860
in a single illuminated patch.

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:28.600
The observation expands known effects of light pollution

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:29.960
beyond flying insects.

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:33.260
Reducing unnecessary outdoor lighting at night

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:34.500
could limit these traps.

00:03:35.140 --> 00:03:38.040
While light alters small animal behavior at night,

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:41.120
researchers have also engineered material shrinkage

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:43.300
to produce functional curved surfaces

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:45.400
inspired by living organisms.

00:03:45.820 --> 00:03:48.420
A programmed shrinkage technique mimics

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:51.680
how flower petals and animal limbs form curved shapes

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:53.560
suited to specific functions.

00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:55.880
The method creates surfaces

00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:58.440
that aid water drainage, improve strength,

00:03:58.820 --> 00:04:00.820
or enhance aerodynamic performance.

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:03.860
Researchers tuned material properties

00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:06.260
to control curvature at multiple scales.

00:04:06.940 --> 00:04:09.500
The approach works with a range of base materials

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:11.780
rather than requiring specialized molds.

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:15.060
Further work will test load bearing capacity

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:18.280
and fluid flow benefits in engineered prototypes.

00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:23.040
A large bio-monitoring study measured 45 environmental chemicals

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:25.680
in maternal blood and associated several

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:28.260
with earlier delivery and lower birth weight.

00:04:28.820 --> 00:04:30.460
Replacement compounds introduced

00:04:30.460 --> 00:04:32.680
after older chemicals were phased out

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:34.260
showed similar associations.

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:37.820
Exposure occurred through everyday products and diet.

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:39.620
The findings highlight the need

00:04:39.620 --> 00:04:42.240
for broader chemical screening during pregnancy.

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:44.920
Follow-up work will examine mixtures

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:46.560
rather than single compounds.

00:04:47.260 --> 00:04:50.300
A registered report tested sequence-based predictors

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:54.500
on a curated set of 3,814 human proteins

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:56.840
with known subcellular locations.

00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:01.280
Performance varied widely across organelles and protein classes.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:04.120
The study provides standardized metrics

00:05:04.120 --> 00:05:06.600
that future algorithms can be measured against.

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:10.100
Independent validation reduced overfitting concerns

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:12.460
common in earlier smaller data sets.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:15.820
Updated predictor versions will be re-evaluated

00:05:15.820 --> 00:05:17.020
on the same benchmark.

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:20.620
An analysis argues that current consent models

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:22.880
overlook patients ongoing control

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:25.620
over their health data after initial collection.

00:05:26.420 --> 00:05:28.960
The authors outline how explicit data rights

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:32.380
could clarify secondary use, sharing, and withdrawal.

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:36.300
The framework aligns with existing privacy regulations

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:38.900
while addressing gaps in research reuse.

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:43.380
Implementation would require changes to electronic health record systems.

00:05:44.060 --> 00:05:47.700
Pilot programs at academic medical centers are under discussion.

00:05:48.560 --> 00:05:51.620
A perspective describes how near-term quantum devices

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:53.960
paired with classical computers could solve

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:56.420
specific molecular simulation problems

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:59.500
before fault tolerant quantum machines arrive.

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:02.140
The approach targets protein folding

00:06:02.140 --> 00:06:05.060
and enzyme design tasks that remain difficult

00:06:05.060 --> 00:06:06.380
for conventional methods.

00:06:07.180 --> 00:06:09.980
Early demonstrations have focused on small molecules,

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:12.540
scaling to clinically relevant proteins

00:06:12.540 --> 00:06:14.680
remains the central engineering challenge.

00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:17.860
Funding agencies are soliciting proposals

00:06:17.860 --> 00:06:20.340
that combine both computing paradigms.

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:24.040
Engineered control over physical form leads naturally

00:06:24.040 --> 00:06:26.320
to questions of evolutionary form.

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:30.100
Analysis of genetic data resolve the longstanding

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:33.120
Zoroptera problem by placing these tiny,

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:37.020
termite-like insects within their correct evolutionary lineage.

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:40.460
The group contains only a few dozen known species

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:43.060
that live under bark or in decaying wood

00:06:43.060 --> 00:06:44.720
and look remarkably similar.

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:47.880
Whole genome comparisons revealed relationships

00:06:47.880 --> 00:06:50.020
hidden by their conserved morphology.

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:53.520
The study integrates fossil and molecular evidence

00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:55.860
to build a clearer insect tree of life.

00:06:56.780 --> 00:06:58.560
Additional sampling of understudy

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:00.680
tropical populations is planned.

00:07:00.680 --> 00:07:03.400
Clarifying hidden relationships in nature

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:06.220
brings us to newly identified shared vulnerabilities

00:07:06.220 --> 00:07:07.760
among gut bacteria.

00:07:08.620 --> 00:07:11.900
Researchers pinpointed enzymes used by E. coli,

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:13.700
shegella and related species

00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:15.660
to penetrate the gut mucus layer.

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:18.840
Blocking these enzymes prevented the bacteria

00:07:18.840 --> 00:07:21.860
from reaching the epithelial surface in animal models.

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:24.800
The common target raises the possibility

00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:27.960
of a single vaccine covering multiple pathogens.

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:31.120
The mechanism centers on mucus degradation

00:07:31.120 --> 00:07:33.080
rather than toxin production.

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:36.580
Human safety studies of candidate inhibitors

00:07:36.580 --> 00:07:38.200
are the next planned stage.

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:41.140
From microbial mechanisms inside the body,

00:07:41.580 --> 00:07:44.700
we turn to a special segment on how everyday lighting

00:07:44.700 --> 00:07:46.720
affects the smallest soil creatures.

00:07:47.540 --> 00:07:49.540
You've probably heard that artificial lights

00:07:49.540 --> 00:07:52.860
at night mainly confuse moths and other flying insects

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:53.900
drawn to bulbs.

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:58.140
In reality, the same lights can trap thousands of pill bugs,

00:07:58.520 --> 00:08:02.240
small ground dwelling crustaceans in endless circular paths.

00:08:02.900 --> 00:08:04.820
Right now, as street lights switch on

00:08:04.820 --> 00:08:06.080
in neighborhoods worldwide,

00:08:06.580 --> 00:08:09.280
wood lights that rely on darkness for orientation

00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:12.020
lose their bearings and loop until exhaustion.

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:15.180
Researchers documented these death spirals

00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:17.200
for the first time in natural settings,

00:08:17.500 --> 00:08:19.980
showing that light pollution reaches even animals

00:08:19.980 --> 00:08:21.900
that never leave the soil surface.

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:24.980
A single illuminated patch can contain

00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:27.640
thousands of trapped individuals illustrating

00:08:27.640 --> 00:08:29.660
how pervasive the effect has become.

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:32.860
The next time you notice outdoor lighting

00:08:32.860 --> 00:08:33.960
left on overnight,

00:08:34.260 --> 00:08:36.980
remember that reducing unnecessary illumination

00:08:36.980 --> 00:08:39.480
protects more than just nocturnal flyers.

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:42.120
It also prevents disorientation

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:43.780
in the smallest soil creatures.

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:46.440
Watch for city lighting ordinances

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:49.100
that incorporate invertebrate behavior data

00:08:49.100 --> 00:08:50.720
alongside energy savings.

00:08:51.720 --> 00:08:54.820
The spacecraft completed a 1 billion kilometer trajectory

00:08:54.820 --> 00:08:58.440
to collect the first asteroid samples for return to Earth.

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:02.140
Onboard instruments will characterize surface composition

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:03.020
before sampling.

00:09:03.740 --> 00:09:06.100
The mission timeline spans more than a year

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:08.360
of crews and proximity operations.

00:09:09.080 --> 00:09:11.460
Data from this encounter will inform models

00:09:11.460 --> 00:09:12.780
of asteroid formation.

00:09:13.520 --> 00:09:16.520
Sample return is scheduled for subsequent mission phases.

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:18.780
A chirping radio signal

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:20.660
from a distant supernova remnant

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:24.020
provided direct evidence that a newly formed magnetar

00:09:24.020 --> 00:09:25.420
can power the explosion.

00:09:26.220 --> 00:09:28.320
The detection used general relativity

00:09:28.320 --> 00:09:31.140
to model the dynamics of the collapsing core.

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:33.640
This marks the initial confirmation

00:09:33.640 --> 00:09:36.300
that such extreme magnetic fields arise

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:38.860
at the moment of neutron star formation.

00:09:39.460 --> 00:09:41.320
Continued monitoring will track

00:09:41.320 --> 00:09:43.880
how the magnetar spin and field evolve.

00:09:44.680 --> 00:09:47.040
The finding refines theoretical predictions

00:09:47.040 --> 00:09:49.040
for the brightest stellar explosions.

00:09:49.700 --> 00:09:52.840
Next time we'll be watching for continued field validation

00:09:52.840 --> 00:09:56.620
of the flockmate sensor system across different sheep breeds.

00:09:57.340 --> 00:09:59.800
That covers today's science and health news.

